.TH version "" "Command"
.SH NAME
version \- print the current directory and date, for use as a build stamp
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBversion\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
version -- print current directory and date
Usage:	version
version takes no arguments; run it inside back-quotes to build a version string.
.HE
.B version
prints, on a single line, the current working directory followed by
the day of the month, the three-letter month abbreviation, and the
last two digits of the year, each field separated by a slash, e.g.
.BR /usr/src/20/Jul/86 .
It takes no arguments and reads no input.
.PP
.B version
is meant to be run inside a back-quote command substitution of the
shell, to stamp a program with the directory and date from which it was
built.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pwd ,
.B date
.SH NOTES
There is no entry for
.B version
in
.BR /etc/helpfile ;
the summary above is written from the source.
